{# THE IDENTITY BAND — structural facts only, byte-identical on every tab and
   on every configure section.

   HOW THE PARK IS SET UP, never what is happening in it. How many stations
   the area registers and how many of them stand a shift, how many rangers
   are stationed at them, how many shifts this area has named, and how many
   stations run on something other than the area's own rules. A live figure
   here would read differently on each of six tabs showing the same minute;
   live figures are the KPI row's job.

   FOUR CELLS, RULED 21 sep against configure-watches.html. The six it
   carried before were the retired model's: rotations per post, the ping
   interval and "generated to" all describe a ring that is no longer how an
   area fills a station, and two of them are now a RULE with its own row on
   the Watches card — a band that repeated them would be a second reading of
   a fact that has one home.

   AND THE VOCABULARY IS STATION, NOT POST. "Rangers 34 posted at 12 posts"
   was the last of that word on this surface.

   `.factband` is the SHELL's component and is not restated in this module's
   sheet — one band, one set of rules, wherever a module draws one.

   EVERY SUB-LINE IS A WHOLE FRAGMENT, and that is not a style note. The
   rangers line once read "posted at the 1" — a sentence with the noun
   missing, which is what happens when a count is dropped into copy written
   for the plural. Each of these reads as a phrase at every count it can
   hold, nought and one included. #}
<div class="factband">
    <span class="f"><span class="k">Stations</span><span class="v">{{ band.stationsInArea }}<em>{% if band.stationsRunningAShift %}{{ band.stationsRunningAShift }} run{{ band.stationsRunningAShift == 1 ? 's' : '' }} at least one shift{% else %}none stands a shift yet{% endif %}</em></span></span>
    {# NO SUB-LINE, on purpose: the label already says what the count is of,
       and the only phrase left to add would repeat the cell beside it. #}
    <span class="f"><span class="k">Rangers stationed</span><span class="v">{{ band.rangers }}</span></span>
    <span class="f"><span class="k">Shifts</span><span class="v">{{ band.namedShifts }}<em>{% if band.namedShifts %}named by this area{% else %}this area has named none{% endif %}</em></span></span>
    <span class="f"><span class="k">Exceptions</span><span class="v">{{ band.stationsWithTheirOwnRules }}<em>{% if band.stationsWithTheirOwnRules == 1 %}station with its own settings{% elseif band.stationsWithTheirOwnRules %}stations with their own settings{% else %}every station follows the area{% endif %}</em></span></span>
    <span class="sp"></span>
    <a class="more" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SETTINGS_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Roster settings &rarr;</a>
</div>
